dfbafc995304ebb9a9b03f65083e6e9cea143b20 Fri Jul 24 18:19:25 2015 +0200 tcp: fix recv with flags MSG_WAITALL | MSG_PEEK
commit dfbafc995304ebb9a9b03f65083e6e9cea143b20
Author: Sabrina Dubroca <sd@queasysnail.net>
Date:   Fri Jul 24 18:19:25 2015 +0200

    tcp: fix recv with flags MSG_WAITALL | MSG_PEEK

    Currently, tcp_recvmsg enters a busy loop in sk_wait_data if called
    with flags = MSG_WAITALL | MSG_PEEK.

    sk_wait_data waits for sk_receive_queue not empty, but in this case,
    the receive queue is not empty, but does not contain any skb that we
    can use.

    Add a "last skb seen on receive queue" argument to sk_wait_data, so
    that it sleeps until the receive queue has new skbs.

    Link: https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=99461
    Link: https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=18493
    Link: https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1205258
    Reported-by: Enrico Scholz <rh-bugzilla@ensc.de>
    Reported-by: Dan Searle <dan@censornet.com>
    Signed-off-by: Sabrina Dubroca <sd@queasysnail.net>
    Acked-by: Eric Dumazet <edumazet@google.com>
    Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>

